Z||000006||turbo86se||06-24-2001||03:46 PM||||hehe, that reminds me of my trip to Maryland last year after the Williamsburg show. I was just checking out the town when I pulled into a Pontiac dealership, the service entrance is right across the street, and one of the mechanics was standing outside, just staring at my black SE. When I exited the dealership, I noticed there were now 7 or 8 mechanics standing outside staring at my Fiero as I pulled away. I slipped the tranny up to N and revved it a little, just letting them know I appreciate the gestures.<P>I should have stopped, maybe next time.||||reg||7
Z||000007||88CoupeV6||06-24-2001||06:02 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by KRMFiero:<BR><B> I saw your car at the Warwick show, I thought your's was one of the nicest i have seen so far... very clean good looking fiero</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Thanks for the compliment. It makes me feel good to hear stuff like that  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. It dose get lots of compliments and turns some heads, but I wish it could do it like my dads vette. Everyone stops to look. My Fiero is so much nicer too. I guess people just don't see what us Fiero people see.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Josh <B>(known by TheFiero64 for first 1239 posts)</B><BR>     <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">    <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||7
